; Parenthesized types.
; - NESTED `(T)` unwraps to `T` (the common case): `nested`'s `(uint)` field is a plain u64.
; - A TOP-LEVEL `foo = (single-type)` is a parenthesized TYPE -> a plain alias (`basic`,
;   `newtype_dropped` -> `pub type ... = u64`). `(A / B)` is a type-choice -> enum.
; - A @-directive on such a parenthesized wrapper is dropped, so `newtype_dropped` is an alias, not a
;   newtype — same as the tagged wrapper `#6.x(...)`. (`holder` references the rules for coverage.)
basic = (uint)
choice = (uint / text)
newtype_dropped = (uint) ; @newtype
nested = [a: (uint), b: tstr]
holder = [ref_basic: basic, ref_choice: choice, ref_newtype: newtype_dropped]
